          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The computer software
            %em Rocq
            (previously called
            = succeed ")" do
              %em Coq
            = succeed "-language" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            and serves in particular as a formal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+management+system"} proof management system
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitions"} definitions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programs"} programs
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorems"} theorems
            together with an environment for semi-interactive development of machine-checked
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/certified+programming"} certified programming
          %p
            The old name,
            = succeed "," do
              %em Coq
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"} Thierry Coquand
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+constructions"} Calculus of Constructions
            (CoC). The new name
            %em Rocq
            originates from
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://www.inria.fr/en"} Inria Rocquencourt
          %h2#applications Applications
          %p
            Computer systems such as Rocq and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
            have been used to give machine-assisted and machine-verified proofs of extraordinary length, such as of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/four-colour+theorem"} four-colour theorem
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kepler+conjecture"} Kepler conjecture
          %p
            More generally, they are being used to formalise and machine-verify large parts of mathematics as such, see the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "#FormalizationOfSetBasedMathematics"} Formalization of set-based mathematics
            below.
          %p
            One striking insight by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
            was that Rocq naturally lends itself also to a formalization of higher mathematics that is founded not on sets, but on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#HomotopyTypeTheory"} Homotopy type theory
          %h3#FormalizationOfSetBasedMathematics Formalization of set-based mathematics
          %p Projects include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ForMath"} ForMath
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#MathClasses"} MathClasses
          %h3#formalized_proofs Formalized proofs
          %p
            Major
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorems"} theorems
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
            have been fully formalized in Rocq include
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feit-Thompson+theorem"} Feit-Thompson theorem
          %h3#HomotopyTypeTheory Homotopy type theory
          %p
            For Rocq-projects in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            see the section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "homotopy+type+theory#Code"} Code
          %h2#RelatedEntries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Rocq uses the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gallina+specification+language"} Gallina specification language
                for specifying
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            %li
              %p
                and it uses a version of the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+constructions"} calculus of constructions
                to implement
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CoqQ"} CoqQ
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+language"} quantum programming language
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+specific+embedded+programming+language"} embedded
                in Rocq.
          %p
            %br/
          %div
            %p
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+assistants"}> proof assistants
                \:
            %p
              based on plain
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Metamath"} Metamath
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mizar"}> Mizar
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NuPRL"} NuPRL
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isabelle"} Isabelle
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HOL"} HOL
            %p
              based on
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rocq"}> Rocq
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lean"} Lean
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arend"} Arend
            %p#BasedOnCubicalTypeTheory
              based on
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/mortberg/cubicaltt"} cubicaltt
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "http://github.com/redprl/redtt"} redtt
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "http://github.com/mortberg/yacctt"} yacctt
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "http://www.redprl.org/en/latest/"} RedPRL
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "Agda#CubicalAgda"} Cubical Agda
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "https://github.com/agda/cubical"} library and demos
                  %li
                    %p
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1lab"} 1lab
                      (cross-linked reference resource)
            %p
              based on
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda-flat"}> Agda-flat
                \:
                %a{:href => "http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~amp12/agda/internal-universes/code/agda-flat/install.txt"} installation instructions
            %p
              based on
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+type+theory"} simplicial type theory
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rzk"} Rzk
            %p
              For
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DisCoPy"} DisCoPy
            %p
              For
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opetopic+type+theory"} opetopic type theory
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Globular"}> Globular
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy.io"} homotopy.io
            %p
              %strong
                projects for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+proof"} formalization
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
                with proof assistants:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archive+of+Formal+Proofs"} Archive of Formal Proofs
                  (using
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isabelle"} Isabelle
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ForMath+project"} ForMath project
                  (using
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rocq"} Rocq
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MathScheme"} MathScheme
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UniMath+project"} UniMath project
                  (using
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rocq"} Rocq
                  and
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xena+project"} Xena project
                  (using
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lean"} Lean
            %p Other proof assistants
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "http://www.andromeda-prover.org/"} Andromeda
            %p Historical projects that died out:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+QED+Project"} The QED Project
          %h2#references References
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://rocq-prover.org/"} Rocq home page
            %li#jsCoq
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://x80.org/rhino-coq/"}> JsCoq
                , a ready-to-use online Rocq environment
            %li#jsHoTTCoq
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://x80.org/rhino-hott/"}> JsHoTTCoq
                , a ready-to-use online
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT"} HoTT
                Coq environment
            %li#CoqWiki
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://coq.inria.fr/cocorico"}> Cocorico
                , the Coq wiki
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/wiki"} HoTT Coq wiki
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/coq/coq/blob/beedccef9ddc8633c705d7c5ee2f1bbbb3ec8a47/dev/doc/README-V1-V5"} history of Coq
            %li
              %p
                Russell O’Connor,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://r6.ca/blog/20091101T231201Z.html"} Believing In-Consistency
              %p
                (On whether the consistency of Coq is believable, given that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+analysis"} ordinal analysis
                techniques are nowhere near able to handle such strong systems.)
          %h3#learning_rocq Learning Rocq
          %p
            To get an idea how to use Rocq from Emacs, there are
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"} Andrej Bauer
            %em Video tutorials for the Rocq proof assistant
            (
            %a{:href => "http://math.andrej.com/2011/02/22/video-tutorials-for-the-coq-proof-assistant/"}> web
            ).
          %p Yet properly learning Rocq can be quite daunting, luckily the right material can help a lot:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benjamin+Pierce"}> Benjamin Pierce
                ‘s
                %a{:href => "http://www.cis.upenn.edu/~bcpierce/sf/"} Software Foundations
                is probably the most elementary introduction to Rocq and functional progamming. The book is written in Rocq so you can directly open the source files in CoqIDE and step through them to see what is going on and solve the exercises.
            %li
              %p
                In a similar style,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"} Andrej Bauer
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                wrote a nice
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/andrejbauer/Homotopy/tree/master/OberwolfachTutorial"} Coq tutorial
                (
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/andrejbauer/Homotopy/blob/master/OberwolfachTutorial/univalence.pdf"}> pdf
                ) on
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#HomotopyTypeTheory"} homotopy type theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+HoTT-Coq+tutorial"} Oberwolfach HoTT-Coq tutorial
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Chlipala"}> Adam Chlipala
                ‘s trimmed down version of
                %a{:href => "http://adam.chlipala.net/papers/CpdtJFR/"} Certified Programming with Dependent Types
                explains more advanced Rocq techniques.
          %h3#applications_to_formal_mathematics Applications to formal mathematics
          %ul
            %li#MahboubiTassi21
              Assia Mahboubi, Enrico Tassi,
              %em Mathematical Components
              (2021) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3999478"}> doi:10.5281/zenodo.3999478
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ForMath"} ForMath
          %ul
            %li#ForMath
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"}> Thierry Coquand
                ,
                %em ForMath: Formalisation of Mathematics
                research project (
                %a{:href => "http://wiki.portal.chalmers.se/cse/pmwiki.php/ForMath/ForMath"}> web
                )
            %li#MathClasses
              %p
                Eelis van der Weegen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"} Bas Spitters
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jelle+Herold"} Jelle Herold
              %p
                %em> Math Classes
                , Coq Library for basic mathematical structures (
                %a{:href => "http://math-classes.org/"}> web
                )
          %p
            Formalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+geometry"} synthetic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+geometry"} Euclidean geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel+Braun"}> Gabriel Braun
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Boutry"} Pierre Boutry
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julien+Narboux"} Julien Narboux
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://geocoq.github.io/GeoCoq/"} GeoCoq
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://gabrielbraun.free.fr/Geometry/Tarski/"} La géométrie de Tarski en Coq
          %p
            Formalization of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories+in+homotopy+type+theory"} internal categories in homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jason+Gross"}> Jason Gross
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Chlipala"} Adam Chlipala
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Spivak"} David Spivak
